<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="025" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>MCP conformance in CI and NFR measurements</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 010, 022, 023 and 024</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies code (.cs test host) and CI workflow; tests/** modified (root CLAUDE.md §8)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>CI wiring and measurement over an existing in-process host, with an explicit suite and spec version</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>H</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns ci-tier1-blocking.yml, the conformance host and McpHostContractTests.cs; 032 touches none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010, 022, 023, 024</deps>
    <tags>ci-cd, testing, integration-test, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Run the modelcontextprotocol/conformance suite (--spec-version 2026-07-28) against /mcp/legal-operations in CI through a test-only host with a test-token injector, add the exact v1 tools/list assertion, and measure NFR-01 (in-process) and NFR-02 at 200 seeded items.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in GitHub Actions, ASP.NET Core test hosts and protocol conformance testing.</role>
  <goal>A blocking CI job runs the conformance suite green; tools/list is asserted to be exactly the five v1 tools; notes/nfr-measurements.md records in-process latency and result sizes at 200 items.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec NFR-09, NFR-01, NFR-02, FR-01 ('tools/list returns exactly the v1 tools'); design §12 (protocol tests, test-token injector). Live NFR-01 latency on the dev BFF is measured in 042.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/Mcp.Conformance.Host/ (test-only console host: runs the BFF via WebApplicationFactory on localhost with a test authentication handler)</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/ci-tier1-blocking.yml (add job mcp-conformance after job 7 `format-changed-cs`, which now ends the file; only after the owner-approved Path-A exception below, otherwise .github/workflows/ci-tier2-advisory.yml)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpHostContractTests.cs (exact five-tool tools/list assertion)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/regression/Mcp/McpResultSizeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/nfr-measurements.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpTestHost.cs (from 020)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.github/workflows/ci-tier1-blocking.yml (existing job structure, e.g. arch-tests L393; job 7 `format-changed-cs` is the model for a Path-A-excepted job: numbered CONTENTS entry in the header plus a job comment block)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">MCP caller-path verification (FR-10 option C) green before conformance and NFR runs</dependency>
      <dependency task="022" status="pending">show and paging tools</dependency>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">plan and lookup tools</dependency>
      <dependency task="024" status="pending">complete tool</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The test authentication handler and token injector exist only under tests/; no file under src/ gains a test-auth path, environment switch or bypass (grep evidence).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The conformance job runs the published modelcontextprotocol/conformance suite pinned to an exact version with --spec-version 2026-07-28 and blocks the PR on failure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">tools/list on /mcp/legal-operations is asserted to be exactly spaarke_show_decisions, the paging tool (final name from 022), spaarke_get_decision_plan, spaarke_search_decision_lookup and spaarke_complete_decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any defect found and not fixed in this task is filed with /project-defer-issue-tracking (notes/defer-issues.md AND a GitHub issue), never one without the other (project CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6.5">Adding a Tier 1 job requires an owner-approved root CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path-A exception to FR-A02: the header of ci-tier1-blocking.yml (L10) says "CONTENTS (strict scope list — do not extend without spec amendment)". Raise 🔔 ADR Conflict before editing the workflow. On approval, add a numbered CONTENTS entry in the header and a job comment block like job 7's (precedents: `xrm-capability-guard`, 2026-10-06; `format-changed-cs`, owner-approved 2026-11-10, PR #2663). Otherwise put the job in ci-tier2-advisory.yml, which does not satisfy NFR-09 'blocking'. Editing the header list without the owner's approval is a blocking error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run `bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master` (blocking Tier 1 'Format (changed C# files)'; fix with `dotnet format whitespace . --folder --include &lt;file&gt;`). CS0618 (obsolete API) is a build error since master 9456083c78: migrate the call or escalate, never suppress it in Directory.Build.props, NoWarn or a file-wide pragma.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/procedures/testing-and-code-quality.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ci-cd/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/FAILURE-MODES.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Create the test-only conformance host under tests/integration/Mcp.Conformance.Host/ that starts the BFF in-process on a localhost port with a test auth handler and seeded fakes.</step>
    <step order="2">Get the owner's §6.5 Path-A exception for a new Tier 1 job (see the constraint), then add the mcp-conformance job to ci-tier1-blocking.yml with its header CONTENTS entry and comment block: build, start the host, run the pinned conformance CLI with --spec-version 2026-07-28, fail on any failure.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the exact five-tool tools/list assertion to McpHostContractTests.</step>
    <step order="4">Add McpResultSizeTests at 200 seeded items for every tool; measure in-process p95 per tool over 50 calls; write notes/nfr-measurements.md.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the job locally (act or the same commands) and in CI.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a conformance failure requires changing SDK behaviour or the transport, STOP and escalate with the failing case.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the suite cannot run without a test-auth path inside src/, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner has not approved a §6.5 Path-A exception to FR-A02 for a new Tier 1 job, STOP before editing the ci-tier1-blocking.yml header and raise 🔔 ADR Conflict; do not extend the CONTENTS list on your own.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No conformance or MCP CI job exists (grep -l conformance .github/workflows returns nothing); tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpTestHost.cs (020) is an in-process xunit host, not an HTTP endpoint the external suite can call.</existing>
    <extension>Partly: the job is added to the existing ci-tier1-blocking.yml rather than a new workflow, which needs the owner-approved Path-A exception to FR-A02 (see constraints); the host project is new because the conformance CLI needs a listening HTTP server.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Protocol regressions (e.g. a broken 2026-07-28 transport behaviour) reach the dev tenant unnoticed, and NFR-09 has no evidence.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
    <tool name="gh">Check CI runs</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">tests/integration/Mcp.Conformance.Host/</output>
    <output type="code">.github/workflows/ci-tier1-blocking.yml</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/regression/Mcp/McpResultSizeTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/nfr-measurements.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The mcp-conformance job runs the pinned conformance suite with --spec-version 2026-07-28 against /mcp/legal-operations and passes in CI (run URL in task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The owner's §6.5 Path-A exception for the new Tier 1 job is cited in the PR, and ci-tier1-blocking.yml has a numbered CONTENTS entry in its header and a job comment block for mcp-conformance; if the exception was not granted, the job is in ci-tier2-advisory.yml and the PR says NFR-09 'blocking' is not met.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: breaking the dual-Accept handling locally (seed) makes the conformance job fail; restored afterwards.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">tools/list is asserted to be exactly the five v1 tools.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At 200 seeded items, every tool result is under 64 KiB (McpResultSizeTests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/nfr-measurements.md records in-process p95 per tool over 50 calls and the largest result size per tool.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file under src/ contains a test-auth handler or bypass (grep evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Pin the conformance package version and record it. Live NFR-01 on the dev BFF (p95 3 s / 1.5 s / 15 s) is measured in 042.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
